<!-- An address-taken stack record read at several widths (P6 stack-frame-layout,
     option stackstruct; P9 pointer-notation, option partialaccess; both default
     off, both on in the aggressive preset).
     Source: decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/fixtures/stack_struct.c, linked with
     stack_struct_helpers.c (gcc -O1 -fno-tree-vectorize -fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns
     -fno-builtin) as `ld -static -e parse_header -Ttext=<base>`; the record is compiled
     with `<cc> -O<n> -fno-pie -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none
     -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -c`: gcc -O0 at 0x401000, gcc -O2 at 0x501000,
     clang -O0 at 0x601000 (.rodata 0x602000), clang -O2 at 0x701000 (.rodata 0x702000).
     header_* passes &h to fetch(&h,8) and setup(&h), then tests the u32 magic, the
     u16 version and the two byte fields. Off: the fields print as Ghidra's
     `v1._4_2_`, which is not C, or (clang -O0) as unrelated scalars. partialaccess
     alone prints the typed pointer access; with stackstruct the record is one
     struct_N whose definition structdefs prints. gcc -O2 and clang -O2 join the
     16-byte vector zero store's two lanes; clang -O0 takes memset's 0x18; gcc -O0
     keeps the later slots separate, since nothing ties them to the record.
     word_sum (one 8-byte word) and text_len (a string built in place) decline. -->
